# Quality Gate Optimization
RULE: Quality gates must complete in <3 minutes. Use pytest-xdist, skip slow tests in quick mode, synthetic fixtures.
WHY: Fast feedback is essential; CI rejects merges without quality gate evidence; skipping Pass 1 causes CI failures.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/quality-gates.md § Two-Pass Workflow Model

Two-pass model — BOTH passes are MANDATORY for agents. Pass 1 cannot be skipped:
- Pass 1 (REQUIRED FIRST): `bash scripts/quality-gates.sh` — full run (lint, tests, typecheck, codex, security)
- Pass 2 (after Pass 1 green): `bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "msg" --agent` — lightweight verify + commit/PR

Flag semantics:
- `--agent` (agent/CI): skip act + skip tests — quickmerge is a fast format/lint/typecheck gate, NOT a substitute for Pass 1
- `--quick` (human only): skip act only — tests still run
- `--agent --skip-typecheck`: lint + format + codex only — only valid if Pass 1 typecheck already passed

DO: Run Pass 1 first always; use pytest-xdist; mark slow tests; `--tb=short`; `--agent` for agent quickmerge
NEVER: Skip Pass 1 and go straight to quickmerge; use `--quick` from agent sessions; use quickmerge as a substitute for quality-gates.sh; exceed 5min total
